From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/videoout: Stretch a picture over the framebuffer when
 PW_PC5_STRETCH=1

A swapchain of a size VideoOut doesn't take (anything but 1920x1080 and
3840x2160) is blitted into framebuffers of the smallest size it takes,
fitted with bars where its shape differs: a 4:3 picture gets bars at its
sides. PC5's Aspect ratio setting can ask for the whole screen instead:
with PW_PC5_STRETCH=1 in the environment the picture is stretched over
the whole framebuffer. The log line says which.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
index 018d12e..552bf2d 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_videoout.c
@@ -1520,11 +1520,18 @@ videoout_surface_create_swapchain(VkIcdSurfaceBase *icd_surface, VkDevice device
    chain->first = set * VIDEOOUT_BUFFERS;
    chain->scaled = scaled;
    chain->target = target;
-   chain->rect = scaled ? wsi_videoout_fit_rect(extent, target) : (VkRect2D){.extent = extent};
+   /* PC5's Aspect ratio: PW_PC5_STRETCH=1 in the environment stretches a picture of
+    * another shape over the whole framebuffer, instead of fitting it with bars. */
+   const char *stretch = getenv("PW_PC5_STRETCH");
+   const bool fill = stretch && stretch[0] == '1' && !stretch[1];
+   chain->rect = !scaled ? (VkRect2D){.extent = extent}
+                 : fill  ? (VkRect2D){.extent = target}
+                         : wsi_videoout_fit_rect(extent, target);
    if (scaled)
       fprintf(stderr,
-              "wsi/videoout: a %ux%u swapchain presents scaled to %ux%u at (%d, %d) of %ux%u framebuffers (set %u)\n",
-              extent.width, extent.height, chain->rect.extent.width, chain->rect.extent.height, chain->rect.offset.x,
+              "wsi/videoout: a %ux%u swapchain presents %s to %ux%u at (%d, %d) of %ux%u framebuffers (set %u)\n",
+              extent.width, extent.height, fill ? "stretched" : "scaled", chain->rect.extent.width,
+              chain->rect.extent.height, chain->rect.offset.x,
               chain->rect.offset.y, target.width, target.height, set);
 
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < num_images; i++) {
